WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.669 --> 00:00:05.520
The reality television series "American Pickers"
has been a constant presence on History's

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:10.610
programming schedule for over a decade, and
remains a fan-favorite show to this day.

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:13.090
"Finally I catch a break."

00:00:13.090 --> 00:00:18.029
Since the series' premiere in January 2010,
the stars of "American Pickers" have traveled

00:00:18.029 --> 00:00:23.240
near and far, searching the United States
for valuable pieces of history housed in shacks,

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:26.270
sheds, shops, storage containers, and more.

00:00:26.270 --> 00:00:30.599
Considering that there's plenty of territory
the stars haven't covered in the show's 22

00:00:30.599 --> 00:00:35.769
seasons, it stands to reason that "American
Pickers" could last another decade or more

00:00:35.769 --> 00:00:36.769
on the air.

00:00:36.769 --> 00:00:41.109
Of course, that depends on whether or not
the network and the series' trio of hosts

00:00:41.109 --> 00:00:45.789
— Mike Wolfe, Frank Fritz, and Danielle
Colby — choose to stick around.

00:00:45.789 --> 00:00:50.749
However, based on the most recent batch of
episodes, that may not be the case.

00:00:50.749 --> 00:00:55.699
Wolfe and Colby were back in action for more
antiquing adventures, but when "American Pickers"

00:00:55.699 --> 00:01:01.519
premiered its 22nd season in January 2021,
Fritz was nowhere to be found.

00:01:01.519 --> 00:01:07.090
He was also absent for the show's midseason
return on June 7th, which got fans talking.

00:01:07.090 --> 00:01:11.820
Discussion about Fritz's Crohn's disease diagnosis
— which explains his recent weight loss

00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:16.810
— prevailed in some circles, while others
pointed to Jersey Jon taking his place as

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:21.033
a sign that Fritz's "American Pickers" tenure
could be coming to an end.

00:01:21.033 --> 00:01:23.500
"No. No. No"

00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:27.689
Here's what we know about Frank Fritz's "American
Pickers" status.

00:01:27.689 --> 00:01:31.869
While there isn't a ton of concrete information
out there about why Fritz has been missing

00:01:31.869 --> 00:01:36.909
from recent episodes, outlets like Celeb Hook
are claiming that there are a few factors

00:01:36.909 --> 00:01:38.939
preventing his immediate return.

00:01:38.939 --> 00:01:44.060
First and foremost, COVID-19 is still a problem,
and since Fritz is someone with a serious,

00:01:44.060 --> 00:01:48.729
pre-existing medical condition, risking catching
the virus is surely something he would want

00:01:48.729 --> 00:01:49.729
to avoid.

00:01:49.729 --> 00:01:54.960
Neither Fritz nor anyone part of the "American
Pickers" team have confirmed this as a reason

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:59.549
for Fritz's absence, but a press release issued
ahead of the show's arrival in Missouri in

00:01:59.549 --> 00:02:05.700
May 2021 reveals that the cast and crew are
taking things seriously regarding COVID-19

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:06.700
safety.

00:02:06.700 --> 00:02:08.300
The press release reads, in part,

00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:13.680
"We understand that with the proliferation
of COVID-19, we are all facing very uncertain

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:14.680
times.

00:02:14.680 --> 00:02:19.470
We at American Pickers are taking the pandemic
very seriously and will be following all guidelines

00:02:19.470 --> 00:02:23.950
and protocols for safe filming as outlined
by the state and CDC."

00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:28.720
The U.S. Sun has also claimed that Fritz was
quarantining in Iowa, where he recently sold

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:30.900
his and his ex-fiancé's home.

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:35.281
It's also worth mentioning that Mike Wolfe
has acknowledged Fritz's disappearance, with

00:02:35.281 --> 00:02:41.099
Reality Titbit reporting Wolfe's announcement
that Fritz underwent back surgery for an undisclosed

00:02:41.099 --> 00:02:42.099
reason.

00:02:42.099 --> 00:02:46.239
Over on the "American Pickers" Facebook page,
one fan confirmed in a comment under a photo

00:02:46.239 --> 00:02:48.030
post in March 2021,

00:02:48.030 --> 00:02:51.949
"[Frank's absence] has been addressed in a
past episode.

00:02:51.949 --> 00:02:53.990
[...] Frank had back surgery, he's recovering."

00:02:53.990 --> 00:02:58.920
The commenter added that in a later episode,
Frank's name was mentioned twice, which should

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:03.329
be proof that he, in their words, "obviously
hasn't been cut out of the show."

00:03:03.329 --> 00:03:07.769
Though it's unclear what Fritz had surgery
for, some types of operations on the back

00:03:07.769 --> 00:03:11.159
or spine can require a lengthy recovery period.

00:03:11.159 --> 00:03:15.829
According to Neurosurgeons of New Jersey,
patients spend at least one day, often more,

00:03:15.829 --> 00:03:20.610
in the hospital immediately after surgery,
then endure between six to eight weeks and

00:03:20.610 --> 00:03:22.439
several months of recovery.

00:03:22.439 --> 00:03:26.540
Patients will likely begin physical therapy
one to three months following surgery, and

00:03:26.540 --> 00:03:31.250
that the frequency, intensity, and overall
duration of therapy sessions differs depending

00:03:31.250 --> 00:03:35.560
on the type of surgery the patient had and
their surgeon's recommendations.

00:03:35.560 --> 00:03:40.540
Having and recovering from back surgery, managing
Crohn's disease, selling a house, and avoiding

00:03:40.540 --> 00:03:46.549
catching and spreading COVID-19 would overwhelm
just about anyone — and Frank Fritz is likely

00:03:46.549 --> 00:03:47.549
no exception.

00:03:47.549 --> 00:03:49.219
"I need a break."

00:03:49.219 --> 00:03:54.140
With COVID-19 vaccination numbers soaring,
according to Bloomberg news, and mask mandates

00:03:54.140 --> 00:03:58.349
being slowly rolled back as well, hopefully
Fritz will feel more comfortable hitting the

00:03:58.349 --> 00:04:02.810
road with his longtime co-host Mike Wolfe
— and digging through America's biggest

00:04:02.810 --> 00:04:05.200
treasure troves in the near future.

